WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.420
Most funnel reports describe last week and stop. This one ends in a decision, and the next one checks whether that decision worked.

2
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:21.870
The report opens with one starred move. This week, thirty one of sixty six new accounts pressed play on the welcome video, forty seven percent against a target of eighty.

3
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:31.200
Every Wednesday at eight in the morning, Central time, the same move leads the email, ahead of the ten numbers that matter most.

4
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:44.100
Attached is a prompt written for Claude Code. It first proves the move is still the right one, then builds it. This move scored forty three point six, the highest this week.

5
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:54.020
In the same pull request, the build appends two entries to a ledger: what changed, and a hypothesis with a number it has to reach.

6
00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:03.320
Every step of the path is held against its own target, so the gap that matters most is easy to see.

7
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:16.340
Of three hundred forty three visitors from the ads, eighty nine signed up for the Open House. That is twenty five point nine percent, against a target of twenty.

8
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:23.940
The flow follows every person from the ad to the first win, and counts people without ever naming them.

9
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:35.700
An earlier move added an Access your account button. Before it, none of five new accounts went in. This week, sixty six of eighty two did.

10
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:46.780
The hypothesis board grades every open test against the new week. That button's test was seventy percent. It reached eighty point five.

11
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:57.560
The ledger becomes the report's timeline. It held fourteen entries by the twelfth of November, and a change of mind is a new entry, never an edit.

12
00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:04.510
It also says what it cannot see yet, and names the next build that would close each gap.

13
00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:19.390
The first edition, about twenty one hours after launch, saw fifty three visitors and no one pressing play. A week later the report had more to measure, and more to remember.

14
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:28.600
One move a week, made by Claude Code and graded the following Wednesday. The report gets more useful every time it runs.
